wineboot looks up no .local host name, so starting a Windows program never waits on the local network.

This repository's patch to wineboot, after the route Ivo Ivanov proposed in Wine bug 60322 (skip the lookup for a
.local name); upstream fixed that bug in Wine 11.19 another way (Hans Leidekker, 724d5ccdbb14, 0be34a3b8fe8 and
4cf90548f2d0: a DNS-only lookup), which still sends a DNS query, to the router on most home networks.

The fault: wineboot runs at every Wine start and, in create_computer_name_keys, asks getaddrinfo for the canonical
name of the Mac's host name, which macOS makes "<LocalHostName>.local" unless a host name is set. A .local name is
answered only by multicast DNS (RFC 6762), and since 0037 every Windows program runs from the engine's mavrik.app,
so macOS puts that query behind its Local Network privacy prompt ("Allow "mavrik" to find devices on local
networks?"). While the prompt was unanswered, each Wine start stalled about 35 s and ws2_32 logged "Failed to resolve
your host name IP" (mavrik S217 lab: wineboot --init 81 s against 14 to 24 s, cmd /c echo 40 s against 5 s).

A name ending in .local (any case) is now used as its own canonical name with no lookup; every other name is looked
up as before. The result is what a failed lookup gave: the DNS host name is the part before the first dot, in the
Mac's own capitals, and the DNS domain "local"; a lookup that answered gave the same name in small letters (DNS names
ignore case). The NetBIOS name (COMPUTERNAME) comes from elsewhere and is unchanged. Games that browse the local
network for multiplayer still ask, as they should.

Checked (mavrik S217 lab, display off, the prompt unanswered, fresh prefixes, interleaved): applies after patches
0001 to 0040 with no fuzz; wineboot builds with the engine's toolchain with no new warning; with the bundle,
wineboot --init took 15.7 and 14.6 s and cmd /c echo 5.0 and 4.9 s with no host-name error, against 89.7 and 80.7 s
and 40.0 and 40.1 s without this patch, and 24.1 and 14.6 s and 5.0 s without the bundle.

diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
index 5e702a5..fb868fe 100644
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -834,7 +834,11 @@ static void create_computer_name_keys(void)
 
     if (gethostname( buffer, sizeof(buffer) )) return;
     hints.ai_flags = AI_CANONNAME;
-    if (getaddrinfo( buffer, NULL, &hints, &res ) != 0)
+    /* A name in .local is answered only by multicast DNS (RFC 6762), which macOS puts behind its
+     * Local Network privacy prompt: while the prompt is unanswered this lookup stalls every Wine
+     * start. Such a name is its own canonical name, so it is used as it is. */
+    if (((dot = strrchr( buffer, '.' )) && !strcasecmp( dot, ".local" )) ||
+        getaddrinfo( buffer, NULL, &hints, &res ) != 0)
         res = NULL;
     else if (res->ai_canonname && strcasecmp( res->ai_canonname, "localhost" ) != 0)
         name = res->ai_canonname;
